        "createdAt": "2026-08-20T10:36:22.790154Z",
        "description": "How Powerhouse chooses where to sell: earn from high-value unscalable consultancy while establishing PMF toward low-value scalable product revenue. An industry qualifies only if it is network-shaped A",
        "orientation": "How Powerhouse chooses where to sell: earn from high-value unscalable consultancy while establishing PMF toward low-value scalable product revenue. An industry qualifies only if it is network-shaped AND already buys consultancy; companion software must be open source, already deployed in those projects, and carry an ecosystem. Manufacturing is the only industry assessed that satisfies every criterion; construction has the connections but no consultancy market, healthcare the reverse. The buyer is the consultancy, not the end client. Read the criteria notes before the per-industry ones - the assessments only make sense against them."
